  "note": "Sky1 arm64 DEFAULT kernel under the unified 7.3 policy: r289 = the COMPLETE v7.3-rc7 port. It is r288 (the mechanical 207-commit kernel-73rc6-port rebase onto v7.3-rc7 + the DP AUX-wedge recovery v2, now folded INTO sky1-ncz-v7.3-rc7-port.patch) PLUS everything r288 was missing because it had branched from the pre-r284 lineage: (a) the r284/r285 review-fix series 0001-0011 (trilin-dp counted OF panel; PCI cadence-sky1-cix ACPI native mode + review fixes; CIX early-boot runtime-PM gate; ACPI fixed-regulator support; ACPI pinctrl defer; cdnsp-sky1 sync_state; audss ACPI parent clocks; pwm_bl CIXH5041 backlight; linlondp DPU-warn; cpufeature SpecSEI non-strict); (b) the r287 CIX q3 vendor sync 0013-0021 (ASoC i2s_mc global-interrupt mask; cdns3/cdnsp RCU-stall, DISABLE_SLOT skip, comp_desc NULL guards; dptx out-of-bound HPD, physical dp->status/MST HPD, eDP-only PSR caps, GOP-plug-after-HDCP; typec rts5453 portX/orientation); (c) CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED is no longer set (the O6N audio-cutout root fix), with the full r283/r285 defconfig set (DMABUF_DEBUG off, DEBUG_INFO_BTF, SQUASHFS_ZSTD, MT7921U/MT7925U/RTW89_8922DE, CRYPTO_ZSTD, I2C_CHARDEV, DRM_PANIC_SCREEN=kmsg). Because RT_GROUP_SCHED changes struct task_struct/sched_rt_entity layout the exported-symbol CRCs moved: ALL SIX committed accelerator overlays (mali_kbase, memory_group_manager, protected_memory_allocator, panthor, aipu, amvx) are REBUILT against the r289 Module.symvers and re-mirrored (verify-overlay-modversions: 0 CRC mismatches, 0 unresolved). Production debs produced by the cix-installer build/build-kernel-debs.sh x2 (byte-identical). The PCIe default is unchanged (sky1_pcie_native=off pcie_pnp_en). The rescue entry boots this same kernel with the arm64 accelerator blacklist. NOT published to the NCZ apt repo (publish-first rule; orchestrator decides after the hardware test). Replaced by 7.3.0 final later.",
